# nr-office-engine-sessions: the session record, the registry and the design binding of sessions (crate mixdog-office,
# module `session`).

The code is in native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/session/{mod,registry,design}.rs and its twin test is
native/core/crates/mixdog-office/tests/twin_sessions.rs (fixture set native/core/fixtures/office-sessions/, recorder
benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-sessions.mjs). It was not compiled by this task (no cargo run): the edits below
to files this task does not own are needed before it can be.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod digest;` add (and one line to the crate doc: `session` is the open document, the registry of open ones and
the design a session is bound to):

    /// The session record, the registry of open sessions and the design a session is bound to.
    pub mod session;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml

[dependencies]: add (both are already [workspace.dependencies] and workspace members; `mixdog-fsio` is already there):

    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-statefile = { workspace = true }

[dev-dependencies]: add (the test runs its file work on the inline durability lane as the design crate's twin tests do):

    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support", "virtual-clock"] }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt"] }

(`mixdog-rt` appears in both tables; the second is the test-only feature set, as mixdog-office-base's manifest writes it.
The tests also use `mixdog-fsio`, `mixdog-js`, `mixdog-office-base` (test-support), `mixdog-office-design` and `tempfile`,
which the crate has.)

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Package `mixdog-office`: its `dependencies` gain `mixdog-rt`, `mixdog-statefile` and `tokio` (all packages of the lock
already; nothing is fetched): `cargo update -w` offline.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Nothing by hand: no new external crate. `tokio` with `rt` is already unified; run the hakari check after the manifest edit
and take what it asks for.

