## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No name to remove: this task registers no service.

## What the later engine tasks and the worker method use

    mixdog_office::session::Registry                       one per engine; clones share the tables
      register(&cx, Session) -> SessionHandle              registerOfficeSession (persists the design binding, then publishes)
      register_handle(&cx, &SessionHandle)                 the same for a session that is already shared
      index / release / for_document / get / remove        indexOfficeSession, releaseOfficeSession, officeSessionForDocument,
                                                           sessions.get, sessions.delete
      ids() -> Vec<String>, documents()                    sessions.keys(), the document index
    mixdog_office::session::ThreadPins                     methods.mjs's sessionsByThread: `let known = ThreadPins::known(&registry)`
                                                           before the call, `pins.finish_call(thread, &known, &registry)` after it
                                                           (answers the `pin` the call returns), `is_pinned(thread)`
    mixdog_office::session::{Session, SessionInit}         the record; `Session::new` is buildOfficeSessionRecord's field part
    mixdog_office::session::{ensure_office_session_design, resolve_office_design_context, merge_office_design_request, EnsureOptions}
                                                           take `&mixdog_office_design::library::Context` (lane, env, fetch,
                                                           template indexer) and the data dir

The template indexer of `Context` is `nr-office-design-templates`'s; until that module is wired the engine passes the one the
wiring provides.

## Left to the tasks that own the neighbouring code

- `args.__signal` is not passed to `resolve_office_design_library` (the library port takes no cancellation); the engine
  checks the call's cancellation around it.
- `buildOfficeSessionRecord`, `pptxReviewDesignState` and `portableCreateDesignState` (office-sessions.mjs) belong to
  nr-office-engine-open-create; they use `Session::new`, `DesignState::empty` and `Session::apply_design_context`.
- The failure of persisting a binding (the warning text carries the operating system's message) is not in the twin; the
  warning path is `design::persist_session_binding`.
